  "pseudos": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "In the heartbroken communities of Deir Ezzor and Raqqa, the life-giving waterway turned destructive after an exceptional deluge. Dams were pushed to their absolute limit, and the surge breached defenses, flooding homes and farms. The river invaded intimate spaces of life, severing a vital link when an earthen bridge collapsed. In the aftermath, rescuers reached out to the stranded as lifesaving operations were launched, while the leader who witnessed the devastation firsthand toured the destruction, a poignant show of solidarity with the affected.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Lover",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "how-4",
          "result-1",
          "result-2",
          "result-5"
        ]
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.65
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "A promise of restraint was made by the upstream nation that agreed to help, a diplomatic agreement reached after the floodwaters broke through. This gesture came in the wake of the ultimate loss of innocent life, as the drowned children were claimed by the uncontrollable flood. The combination of human action and nature's force had overwhelmed water storage, leaving the river to consume the suffering city and its sister region, a story of broken trust and fragile bonds between nations and the land.",
